\ ff-test: lines
\ A `(` comment whose `)` is the last byte of the line.
\
\ A closing paren at the very end of the text given to ff_eval() - a line
\ from an interactive host - used to read as an unclosed comment: the
\ cursor sat at the end either way. The comment then ran on and swallowed
\ the lines after it, up to a `)` with text behind it.

( one line )
1 . cr
( two
lines )
2 . cr
( open
still open
) 3 . cr
: sq ( n -- n*n ) dup * ;
4 sq . cr
